# func/text/tx_case (id 314): UPPER / LOWER core. A = text or error; N0 = 0 UPPER, 1 LOWER.
# Result A = (2, new handle) or the error unchanged. Maps a..z and Latin-1 letters U+00E0..U+00FE
# (not U+00F7) to upper case, or A..Z and U+00C0..U+00DE (not U+00D7) to lower case.
# PC 0: error -> return; else read [h], P0 = h + 2, P1 = HT + 2, T1 = HT (new handle), PC 1.
# PC 1: write [T1] = length, N1 = length, PC 2. PC 2: N1 <= 0 -> A = (2, T1), HT = P1, return;
# else read [P0], PC 3. PC 3: write [P1] = mapped word, P0 += 1, P1 += 1, N1 -= 3, PC 2.
